  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1105 AM MDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\n16z surface analysis had weak low over the NE panhandle with a \nboundary into central SD per 0.5km 1-minute visible satellite \nloop. Cold front was located from western ND into western WY. \nWater vapour loop had shortwave trough over northern WY with 80kt \njet streak. These features starting to force CU/TCU/TS along the \nsurface boundary with evidence of decent lift ahead of the \nshortwave over northeastern WY/eastern MT. Concern this \nafternoon/evening is severe weather.\n\nThis afternoon/evening, shortwave trough moves east as \nconvergence along the surface boundaries increase. Mid-level flow \nincreases effective shear to 25-35kts with locally higher amounts \nover central SD. Strong buoyancy will develop this afternoon, \nespecially east of the Black Hills. Initial storm mode may be \ncellular with large hail potential, but the trend will be toward \nsevere clusters/linear severe convection as storm cold pools \ncongeal. Primary threat will be damaging winds gusts (70+ mph). \nLooking for a fairly early start this afternoon with CAMs focusing\non the central/southern Black Hills and central SD this afternoon\nand then Lemmon to Winner by evening as the main shortwave wraps \nthrough the CWA. PWATs will be 150-200% of normal east of the\nBlack Hills, so locally heavy rain and potential flash flooding\nmay occur. Activity wanes overnight. Temperatures will be near \nguidance.\n\nA weak shortwave moves through Friday, but drier air will be \nfiltering into the CWA, so PoPs should be limited to our higher \nterrain areas.\n\nHot to very hot weather returns for the weekend with the \npreponderance of ensemble guidance giving highs near 110F for some\nfolks Sunday. Much drier air in place, so thunderstorm chances \nwill be unmentionable. Cooler weather returns Monday with actual \n\"cool\" air in place for the middle of next week per flattening \nupper ridge and west/northwest flow aloft for the northern Plains.",
